  "question": "1) Background / Context\n\nThe project involves developing an administration platform using Laravel, leveraging Orchid—a comprehensive solution for creating admin panels and back-office applications. This platform will serve as a foundation for building content management systems and line-of-business applications with rapid and efficient development.\n\n2) Objectives\n\nThe primary goal is to enable the creation of robust administration applications by providing a framework that emphasizes code-driven development. The system should facilitate efficient handling of UI components, user permissions, and file attachments.\n\n3) Stakeholders & Users\n\n- Developers: Use the platform to build and customize admin applications.\n- Administrators: Manage user roles, permissions, and content.\n- End Users: Access application features according to assigned roles and permissions.\n\n4) Functional Descriptions\n\n- UI Components: Provide an extensive array of UI elements such as form inputs, dialogs, data grids, and visualizations. Ensure these components can be extended and composed directly in the code.\n  \n- Permissions Management: Facilitate seamless management of user roles and permissions through an intuitive interface, ensuring application security without the need for complex coding.\n\n- File Attachments: Enable attaching various file formats to application records, supporting organized data management and streamlined workflow for users.\n\n- Role Management: Implement a robust mechanism for users to be assigned multiple roles, linking users with roles and permissions as defined in the `roles` table and its relationships.\n\n5) Non-Functional Descriptions\n\n- Performance: Ensure the platform can handle efficient creation and management of admin panels without significant latencies, leveraging Laravel's inherent capabilities.\n\n- Scalability: Design the system to support scalable growth in terms of number of users and attached files, ensuring the underlying architecture supports expansion.\n\n- Security: Enforce strong security measures, particularly in permissions management, to protect sensitive data and operations.\n\n- Usability: Offer a straightforward and intuitive interface for developers and administrators, facilitating ease of use in building and managing applications.\n\n- Reliability: Ensure data integrity and consistent performance, especially concerning the attachment, storage, and retrieval of files as well as notification handling.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0066\nCREATE TABLE `users` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `remember_token` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `users_email_unique` (`email`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `roles` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `slug` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `permissions` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `roles_slug_unique` (`slug`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user_roles` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `role_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  KEY `user_roles_user_id_index` (`user_id`),\n  KEY `user_roles_role_id_index` (`role_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `user_roles_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `user_roles_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`role_id`) REFERENCES `roles` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `attachments` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `attachable_type` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `attachable_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `disk` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `path` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `original_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `mime_type` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `size` bigint(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  KEY `attachments_user_id_index` (`user_id`),\n  KEY `attachments_attachable_index` (`attachable_type`,`attachable_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `attachments_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE SET NULL ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `notifications` (\n  `id` char(36) NOT NULL,\n  `type` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `notifiable_type` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `notifiable_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `data` text NOT NULL,\n  `read_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  KEY `notifications_notifiable_index` (`notifiable_type`,`notifiable_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
